{"title":"Velocity","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Velocity</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vector\" title=\"Vector\">vector</a> quantity, defined by the speed at which an object is traveling (its magnitude) and the direction at which it is traveling. It is also the first <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Derivative\" title=\"Derivative\">derivative</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Displacement\" title=\"Displacement\">displacement</a>.\n</p><p>It shouldn't be confused with speed, as speed is a scalar, the first derivative of distance. However, velocity can be considered as the product of speed and the unit tangent vector -- the instantaneous direction of the object.\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Velocity&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017220342\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.010 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 7/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 265/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.182      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.182      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6921:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017220342 and revision id 240120. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}